GeneID:57147, pseudokinase 3
Pseudokinase 3 (PNKP) is a gene in humans that encodes a protein involved in DNA repair processes. PNKP functions as a pseudokinase, meaning it has a kinase-like domain but lacks the typical catalytic activity of a true kinase. It plays a crucial role in repairing DNA strand breaks, particularly in the repair of single-strand breaks in DNA. PNKP is involved in the base excision repair (BER) pathway and helps maintain genomic stability. Mutations in PNKP can lead to disorders such as neurodegeneration with brain iron accumulation (NBIA), as well as other neurodegenerative diseases.

