"GeneID:2326" flavin containing dimethylaniline monoxygenase 1
Flavin-containing dimethylaniline monoxygenase 1 (FMO1) is a gene in humans that encodes an enzyme involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics and endogenous compounds. FMO1 is a member of the flavin-containing monooxygenase (FMO) family, which catalyzes the oxidation of nitrogen, sulfur, and phosphorus-containing compounds. Specifically, FMO1 plays a significant role in the oxidation of dimethylaniline and other substrates, facilitating their detoxification. It is predominantly expressed in the liver and kidneys. Variations in FMO1 expression or activity have been linked to differences in drug metabolism and susceptibility to certain toxins, though its activity is less studied compared to other FMO isoforms like FMO3.

